{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2790,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The idea that certain things, events or people\ncan “cause” other things to happen plays"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7400,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a huge role in human life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9470,
    "dDurationMs": 5430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We constantly desire to know “why” things\nhappen, in science, love, sports, philosophy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14900,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15900,
    "dDurationMs": 3749,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because the underlying laws of physics\ndon’t care about the direction of time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19649,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cause and effect don’t have the same meaning\nat a fundamental level."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22489,
    "dDurationMs": 1781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s not that anything goes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24270,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The basic constituents of the universe -- the\nparticles and forces of modern physics -- behave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28550,
    "dDurationMs": 3010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in predictable ways according to the laws\nof nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31560,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In principle, you can just as easily know\ntheir past paths as their future ones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35910,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The current momentum and position of a particle\ndetermine its movement forward in the next"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40460,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "second, but they also determine how it was\nmoving in the previous second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44170,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Neither is really a “cause” preceding\nan “effect”, there’s just a pattern"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47620,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that particles follow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48760,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kind of like how the integer after 42 is 43,\nand the integer before it is 41, but 42 doesn’t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54960,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“cause” 41 or 43 – there’s just a\npattern traced out by those numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59480,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At a fundamental, microscopic level, all we\ncan say is that there are patterns between"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63730,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "events."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64730,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The macroscopic, human-scale concepts of cause\nand effect only emerge when you have larger"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69370,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collections of particles, like humans!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71850,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As we know, time does have a direction for\nlarger-scale systems, and we can indeed talk"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75950,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about a spark causing oxygen and hydrogen\nto turn into water and an explosion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80530,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“Spark plus oxygen plus hydrogen” and\nthen “water plus explosion” is a sequence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85590,
    "dDurationMs": 3190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the universe follows, and it only happens\nin one direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88780,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You never see a reverse explosion where water\nspontaneously splits into oxygen and hydrogen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93220,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gas and then at the very end emits a little\nspark."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96340,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One way of thinking about causes is that the\ntiny spark has great “leverage” over the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100760,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "future."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101760,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you hadn’t lit the spark, we wouldn’t\nhave seen a giant explosion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104700,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It doesn’t work the other way: removing\nor changing a tiny part of the giant explosion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109680,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn’t imply that there wasn’t a preceding\nspark."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112830,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When a small change to the present implies\na big change to the future, the small thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117380,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we’re changing is generally thought of as\na “cause”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120380,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Leverage can also go the other way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121970,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take this new pencil: the wood it’s made\nof contains trace amounts of radioactive carbon-14,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126740,
    "dDurationMs": 1670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "created by nuclear bomb testing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128410,
    "dDurationMs": 4689,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the pencil didn’t contain that carbon-14,\nthat would imply that no nuclear bombs had"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133099,
    "dDurationMs": 4431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been detonated in the last 80 years; while\nif you removed a pencil-sized amount of one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137530,
    "dDurationMs": 3579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the atomic bombs, this pencil would still\nbe basically the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141109,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, the fact that the pencil has\nlots of carbon 14 means that it has a lot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145159,
    "dDurationMs": 1881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of “leverage” over the past."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147040,
    "dDurationMs": 4429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of calling the carbon 14 in this pencil\na “cause” of the earlier detonation of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151469,
    "dDurationMs": 3321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hundreds of nuclear bombs, we call it a “record”\nof the bombs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154790,
    "dDurationMs": 4539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In general, when a small change to the present\nwould imply a big change to the past, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159329,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "small thing we’re changing is thought of\nas a “record” or a “memory”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162749,
    "dDurationMs": 3541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the distinctions between “cause” and\n“effect”, “records” and “predictions”,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166290,
    "dDurationMs": 5179,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aren’t fundamental to underlying physics\n– they only really make sense on the large"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171469,
    "dDurationMs": 34190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scale, because of the direction of time."
    } ]
  } ]
}
